Third-party material
--------------------

LegacyLyrion A200 is built with, but does not include, the following. The
build scripts download them from Maven Central into lib/, which is not part
of this repository:

- Eclipse Compiler for Java (ECJ) 4.6.1, by the Eclipse Foundation
  (https://www.eclipse.org/jdt/core/), licensed under the Eclipse Public
  License 1.0: https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-v10.html
- MicroEmulator 2.0.4 CLDC 1.1 and MIDP 2.0 API jars, by Bartek Teodorczyk
  and the MicroEmulator team (https://github.com/barteo/microemu), licensed
  under the GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 or the Apache License 2.0:
  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The files in stubs/ are minimal compile-time stand-ins for the JSR-256
Mobile Sensor API, the Nokia UI API's DeviceControl class and the JSR-226 SVG
API, written for this
project from the public API signatures. They are never packaged; the phone
provides the real implementations.

Spotify browsing and playback rely on the Spotty plugin for Lyrion Music
Server by Michael Herger (https://github.com/michaelherger/Spotty-Plugin),
which builds on librespot (https://github.com/librespot-org/librespot).
LegacyLyrion A200 does not include any Spotty code; it talks to the plugin
through Lyrion's standard controller (Jive) menus. Spotty must be installed
separately on the Lyrion server, and is credited and licensed by its own
authors.

YouTube Music browsing and playback rely on the YouTube Music for LMS plugin
by schmij97 (https://github.com/schmij97/lms-ytmusic), which uses yt-dlp
(https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp). LegacyLyrion A200 does not include any
of its code; it talks to the plugin through the same Jive menus. The plugin
must be installed separately on the Lyrion server.

The menu logic (Jive items and command building) follows LegacyLyrion for
Android (https://github.com/h33ted/LegacyLyrion) by the same author.

The visual style is drawn entirely in code (src/ll/Style.java) in the manner
of Sony Ericsson's own 2009 media applications; it contains no Sony Ericsson
artwork.

